From: Ben Klopfenstein <benklop@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Let SDL2 pick the video driver when SDL_VIDEODRIVER names an
 SDL 1.2 console driver

Launchers written for real SDL 1.2 on a framebuffer console export
SDL_VIDEODRIVER=fbcon. sdl12-compat hands the name to SDL2, which has no
such driver, and the app fails with "fbcon not available".

Treat the SDL 1.2 console drivers SDL2 never had (fbcon, svgalib, dga) as
"no preference": an empty hint makes SDL2 choose a driver itself, which on
Calculinux is kmsdrm.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Calculinux-specific]

diff --git a/src/SDL12_compat.c b/src/SDL12_compat.c
index 7942ff4..42717d3 100644
--- a/src/SDL12_compat.c
+++ b/src/SDL12_compat.c
@@ -2835,6 +2835,16 @@ SDL_InitSubSystem(Uint32 sdl12flags)
        have this problem, so we're ignoring the parachute until a reasonable
        need arises. */
 
+    /* SDL 1.2 video drivers that SDL2 doesn't have. Launchers written for
+       real SDL 1.2 on a framebuffer console force these; SDL2 would fail
+       with "fbcon not available". An empty hint lets SDL2 choose. */
+    if (videodriver &&
+        (SDL20_strcmp(videodriver, "fbcon") == 0 ||
+         SDL20_strcmp(videodriver, "svgalib") == 0 ||
+         SDL20_strcmp(videodriver, "dga") == 0)) {
+        videodriver = "";
+    }
+
     #define SETFLAG(flag) { \
         const Uint32 f12 = SDL12_INIT_##flag; \
         const Uint32 f20 = SDL_INIT_##flag; \
